            <ArticleTitle>Pneumocephalus following an epidural blood patch.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>907-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pneumocephalus is a rare complication of epidural block. We report a case of pneumocephalus complicating an epidural blood patch performed 3 days after unintentional dural puncture. Pneumocephalus may occur during an epidural blood patch procedure, even if the epidural needle tip is within the epidural space.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
